From d64fb2f92ab8e255849b8faec490ff5faad07f81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 07:20:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix T_right dead-end starvation: density is redundant
 evidence, not mandatory

Real upstream commit 9f74b2b8 (a completed 14000-step run from the prior
session, discovered only after rebasing onto it -- my local checkout had
been seeded from an earlier snapshot) found that T_right, the last-queued
branch, never reaches dead-end confirmation: local density plateaus at a
genuine steady state of 0.61, permanently below KHOP_DEAD_END_DENSITY_RATIO
(0.70), while clearance (2.8, at the wall) and contact compression (0.426,
above the 0.28 floor) both already show real crowding.

update_khop_dead_end_detection required density_observed as a separate
hard AND alongside compression_observed (pressure OR contact), so a
branch whose corridor geometry happens to read a lower density ratio for
the same physical jam (density is area-normalized; a wider corridor
spreads identical crowding over more area) could satisfy every other
condition and still never confirm. Folded density into the same
three-way OR as pressure/contact instead of requiring it in addition to
them -- clearance and forward_speed stay hard gates (the front must
genuinely be at the wall and stopped), but any one of density/pressure/
contact now independently proves crowding, matching the multi-signal-
redundancy the round-3 fix intended rather than re-adding a single point
of failure.

Verification (fresh 14000-step run with this fix plus the previously
committed normalization change) is running in the background as of this
commit.

